{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.GCTMultiplicityObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.GCTMultiplicityObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hard_ne_easy_of_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hard_ne_easy_of_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L76-L86","doc":"**Conditional consequence (sorry-free): given the bridge, `hard ≠ easy` at\nevery `n`.**  A rigorous *conditional* GCT result: **if** the\nresolution-tree obstruction is a per-`n` multiplicity obstruction, **then**\nthe hard and easy objects have distinct multiplicity data at every scale —\nthe separation the program targets.  Everything here is proven modulo the\nsingle open class instance (the GCT obstruction existence), which is the\nactual mathematical content and stays absent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QouGCTObstruction.obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QouGCTObstruction.obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L74-L74","doc":"For every `n`, some partition is a multiplicity obstruction separating\nthe hard object from the easy one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QouGCTObstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QouGCTObstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QouGCTObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QouGCTObstruction","kind":"class","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L61-L74","doc":"**The QOU–GCT bridge (conjecture; NO instance — GCT is open).**  Conjectures\nthat for each `n` the resolution-tree obstruction is realised as a\n*multiplicity obstruction* at some partition `λ_n` separating the\ncounting-hard object `hard n` from every poly-time object `easy n`.  The\nclass field carries the per-`n` obstruction as genuine content; **no\ninstance is provided** — a fabricated one would be a `P`-vs-`NP` (indeed\n`VP`-vs-`VNP`) separation.  The QOU's concrete candidate for the\nmultiplicity drop is the Temperley–Lieb stratification\n(`WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_eq_zero_iff`): at physical `X = Q^{-N}`\nthe content-`N` Schur elements vanish, dropping those `λ`-multiplicities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_both_mem_of_separatedAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_both_mem_of_separatedAt","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L50-L59","doc":"**Class separation from a multiplicity obstruction (sorry-free).**  If a\ncomplexity class `C` is *multiplicity-closed* — any two members agree at\n`λ` — then a multiplicity obstruction at `λ` places `A`, `B` in different\nclasses: they cannot both lie in `C`.  This is the GCT strategy in one\nline: for each `n` exhibit a `λ` on which the hard and easy objects'\nmultiplicities differ, and no class contains both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.multData_ne_of_separatedAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.multData_ne_of_separatedAt","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**A multiplicity obstruction is a genuine separator (sorry-free).**  A\nsingle `λ` with differing multiplicity forces the whole multiplicity data\nto differ — the foundational GCT step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SeparatedAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SeparatedAt","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L39-L41","doc":"`A` and `B` are **GCT-separated at `λ`** when their `λ`-multiplicities\ndiffer — a *multiplicity obstruction* at `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.MultData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.MultData","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GCTMultiplicityObstruction.lean#L34-L37","doc":"**Multiplicity data** of an object: each partition (irrep label) ↦ its\nmultiplicity. In the QOU these are the Wedderburn/SYT multiplicities of the\ncategorical decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}